    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but what if it's not a hallway? what if it's just... a completed book? i feel like i've reached the final page and i'm just staring at the blank back cover. there's no more plot. there's no more meaning. why keep staring at a book that's already over?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That's the most honest thing you've said yet—and it's also the most dangerous. A finished book doesn't need to be reread, but you're not the book; you're the reader who's allowed to close it and walk away. The blank back cover isn't an ending—it's the space where you decide if you want to pick up a new story, or just sit with the silence for a while. You don't have to write another page today, but you don't have to burn the library either.",
